qualities:
  - id: 24f8d6cc-9f2d-44e1-9c78-5cbb438bbadc
    name: '''Mentor Spirit: Fire Bringer'''
    type: positive
    description: |-
      he Fire-Bringer stole the secret of fire from the heavens and gave it to metahumanity as a
            gift and a tool. He is a figure of kindness and concern, but his good intentions sometimes
            get him into trouble and his plans sometimes fail to work out the way he envisions them. He
            is a shaper and a creator, forming new things from the primal clay and breathing the fiery
            spark of life into them. Fire-Bringers devote themselves to the betterment of others, even at
            their own expense. Most Fire-Bringer magicians devote themselves to a particular cause they
            follow with great zeal.
            Advantages: +2 dice for Manipulation spells, +2 dice for fire spirits.
            Disadvantages: –1 die for Illusion spells.
    effects:
      - type: skillSpecializationMod
        target: Spellcasting
        value: 2
        subTarget: Manipulation Spells
      - type: skillSpecializationMod
        target: Spellcasting
        value: -1
        subTarget: Illusion Spells
      - type: skillSpecializationMod
        target: Banishing
        value: 2
        subTarget: Spirits of Spirit of Fire
      - type: skillSpecializationMod
        target: Binding
        value: 2
        subTarget: Spirits of Spirit of Fire
      - type: skillSpecializationMod
        target: Summoning
        value: 2
        subTarget: Spirits of Spirit of Fire
    bpValue: 5
    source:
      book: SR4A
      page: 94
    kind: quality
  - id: b271b9bd-1c8a-4deb-b1db-714bf035f5b2
    name: Astral Beacon
    type: negative
    description: |2-
            The astral signature of a character with the Astral Beacon quality
            sticks out like a sore thumb on the astral plane. All signatures left by the
            character last twice as long, and others assensing the signature receive
            a +2 dice pool modifier. Only characters with the Adept, Magician, or
            Mystic Adept qualities may take this quality.
    effects: []
    bpValue: 5
    source:
      book: SR4A
      page: 94
    kind: quality
  - id: 6194666d-4f96-451d-98f8-e8631a69e080
    name: Sensitive System
    type: negative
    description: |2-
            A character with the Sensitive System quality has immuno-sup-
            pressive problems with implants. Double all Essence losses caused by
            cyberware implants. This quality does not affect Essence losses for
            bioware.
    effects: []
    bpValue: 15
    source:
      book: SR4A
      page: 95
    kind: quality
  - id: 64203a4d-f6ef-4c3e-947d-a42e085239b7
    name: Wanted (Renraku)
    type: negative
    description: >-
      "For some reason (defined when the quality is taken), the character is wanted by the authorities, has a bounty on
      her head, or a mob contract hanging over her. Such bounties/contracts should be worth at least 20,000 nuyen.
      Unlike characters with Enemies, a Wanted character is not constantly harassed by a single opponent\n(though the
      two can be combined). Instead, she will be hunted by anyone who becomes aware of the bounty and is interested in
      collecting\nit. It is up to the gamemaster how much this quality impacts the game, but, as a rule of thumb, it
      should come up at least once every other adventure. The is quality may not be bought out , until the reason the
      character is wanted is resolved through role-playing."
    effects: []
    source:
      book: RC
      page: 110
    bpValue: 10
    kind: quality
